mind your decisions i'm presh talwalkar  the first term of an infinite series is  one divided by five root four plus four  root five  the second term is one divided by six  root five plus five root six  the pattern continues indefinitely  what is the value of this infinite  series  i was suggested this problem by a  student in indonesia  pause the video if you'd like to give  this problem a try and when you're ready  keep watching to learn how to solve this  problem  [Music]  a general term in this series is 1  divided by n multiplied by the square  root of n minus 1  plus n minus 1 multiplied by the square  root of n  we can simplify this fraction with the  classic trick of multiplying the  numerator and denominator by the  conjugate  the result will be a difference of  squares  we'll take the square of the first term  minus the square of the second term  this is the resulting fraction  we can then factor the denominator by  factoring the quantity n multiplied by n  minus 1.  we then simplify the denominator  we now have a single term in the  denominator so we can divide through  we end up with the following result  it'll be equal to the square root of n  minus 1  over n minus 1 minus the square root of  n over n  we will use this formula to simplify  each term in the series we'll apply this  formula to the first term  here n is equal to five  we thus get the result of the square  root of four over four  minus the square root of five over 5.  we apply the formula to the second term  here n is equal to 6.  then we apply this formula to the third  term and here n is equal to 7.  this pattern continues indefinitely  we'll simplify the result  notice we have a negative square root of  5 over 5 plus a square root of 5 over 5  and these two terms will cancel  the following two terms will also cancel  and this pattern will continue  indefinitely  the only term that survives is the very  first term  this is reminiscent of a telescope that  retracts upon itself  for this reason this type of sum is  known as a telescoping sum  all of the terms vanish except the very  first term  this simplifies to be 2 over four which  is equal to one half and that's our  answer  it's a pretty radical and neat sum  thanks for making us one of the best  communities on youtube see you next  episode of mind your decisions where we  solve the world's problems one video at  a time  [Music]  you
 

